## Context 

We would like to add the following two APIs to the C++ frontend:

*  `torch::nn::TripletMarginLoss` , which is the equivalent of Python API `torch.nn.TripletMarginLoss`.
* `torch::nn::functional::triplet_margin_loss`, which is the equivalent of Python API `torch.nn.functional.triplet_margin_loss`.



## Steps

* Add `torch::nn::TripletMarginLossOptions` to `torch/csrc/api/include/torch/nn/options/loss.h` (add this file if it doesn’t exist), which should include the following parameters (based on https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/nn.html#torch.nn.TripletMarginLoss)
    * `TORCH_ARG(double, margin) = 1.0`
    * `TORCH_ARG(double, p) = 2.0`
    * `TORCH_ARG(double, eps) = 1e-6`
    * `TORCH_ARG(bool, swap) = false`
    * `TORCH_ARG(Reduction::Reduction, reduction) = Reduction::Mean`
    * NOTE: please make sure to add the same comments for the parameters as in the Python version. For example, for parameter `p` we should say `The norm degree for pairwise distance. Default: 2`.
* Add `torch::nn::functional::triplet_margin_loss(...)` in  `torch/csrc/api/include/torch/nn/functional/loss.h` (add this file if it doesn’t exist). The function should have the following signature:

```
namespace torch {
namespace nn {
namespace functional {

inline Tensor triplet_margin_loss(
    const Tensor& anchor,
    const Tensor& positive,
    const Tensor& negative,
    const TripletMarginLossOptions& options = {}) {
  ...
}

} // namespace functional
} // namespace nn
} // namespace torch
```

* Add `torch::nn::TripletMarginLoss` in `torch/csrc/api/include/torch/nn/modules/loss.h` (add this file if it doesn’t exist). The module’s constructor should take `torch::nn::TripletMarginLossOptions` as input (and store it in its internal options field), and the module’s forward method should have the following signature:

```
Tensor forward(
    const Tensor& anchor,
    const Tensor& positive,
    const Tensor& negative) {
  // Should call torch::nn::functional::triplet_margin_loss with all inputs and the module's options
